Gears of War 3: block-compressed textures are never taken as scaled resolves. Resolves cannot write
DXT, so such a texture in memory that was a resolve destination earlier holds data the CPU loaded.
As a scaled resolve it skipped the texture pack: at 2x the button prompt atlases went back to the
original Xbox 360 glyphs after checkpoint reloads.

diff --git a/src/graphics/pipeline/texture/cache.cpp b/src/graphics/pipeline/texture/cache.cpp
